1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
This free kick bent so much… a ball boy ducked.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,300
And the goalkeeper didn’t even move.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:10,400
June 3, 1997. Lyon, France.

4
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:14,400
Brazil against France.

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,800
21 minutes. A free kick, almost 40 yards from goal.

6
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:21,900
Roberto Carlos walks back… 18 steps.

7
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:25,100
He runs in and hits it with the outside of his left foot.

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:30,700
The ball flies past the wall… so wide that a ball boy, way off to the right, ducks.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:37,150
Then it swerves. Back towards the goal… off the post… and in.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,800
The goalkeeper, Fabien Barthez, never moved.

11
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:43,300
For years, people called it a fluke.

12
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:46,300
In 2010, French physicists explained it:

13
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:52,900
hit hard enough, from far enough, a spinning ball curls more and more… in a spiral.

14
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:55,900
So, luck… or physics?

15
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,600
Tell me in the comments.
